  "text": "Economic Impacts | Mississippi State University Extension Service Skip to main content Skip to main menu Skip to footer Join the Magnolia Moves Activity Challenge! Site search Home About Extension Economic Impacts Economic Impacts Extension grows Mississippi’s economy through education and service in 4-H, agriculture and natural resources, government and community development, and family, health, and wellness. Extension clients benefit from learning the research-based information we present, and we’re generating millions in cost savings and profits across the state. M2480-01 Reducing Unnecessary Input Costs for Soybean Farmers M2480-02 Managing Insect Pests of Cotton– Tarnished Plant Bug M2480-03 Meeting the Needs of Mississippi Peanut Producers M2480-04 Row Crop Short Course Supports Producers and Industry M2480-05 Helping Rice Producers Control Weeds M2480-06 Preserve It, Don’t Waste It: The Money-Saving Power of Canning M2480-08 Mississippi Master Gardeners Extend University Knowledge M2480-09 Mississippi Homemaker Volunteers Strengthen Communities M2480-10 4-H Volunteers Mentor and Educate State's Youth M2480-11 Corn Seed Hybrid Trials Increase Profits M2480-12 Cotton Seed Variety Trials Improve Yields M2480-13 EFNEP Supports Nutrition-Insecure Adults M2480-15 Coastal Cleanup Program M2480-16 Mississippi Master Naturalist Volunteer Program M2480-17 Natural Resources Enterprises Program M2480-18 Soybean Seed Variety Trials M2480-19 Soybean Variety Trials (2015-2024) M2480-20 Cotton Variety Trials (2024 Crop Year) M2480-21 Cotton Variety Trials (2015–2024 Crop Years) M2480-22 Rice Variety Trials (2023) M2480-23 Corn Hybrid Trials (2015-2024 Crop Years) M2480-24 Catfish Production Program M2480-25 Protect and Connect: A Child Maltreatment Prevention Program M2480-26 Parenting Interventions: TBRI with Court-Involved Families M2480-27 MSU Extension Head Start Program M2480-28 Nurturing Homes Initiative M2480-29 Mississippi LIFT Resource & Referral Network 